### 📐 Indicator Calculation Methodology

#### ⏱️ 1. Idling Time Reduction ($T_{\text{saved}}$)
* **Definition:** Measures the net hours of staging queue delay eliminated per cleared freight unit.
* **Calculation:**
  $$T_{\text{saved}} = T_{\text{baseline}} - T_{\text{pass}}$$
* **Variables & Inputs:**
  * $T_{\text{baseline}} = 42.50\text{ hours}$ (Uncoordinated Dorohusk staging queue baseline).
  * $T_{\text{pass}} = 0.50\text{ hours}$ (Automated 3-Gate clearance pass time).
  * **Net Impact:** **42.00 hours saved per express transit**.

#### ⛽ 2. Fuel Consumption & Auxiliary Burn Saved ($\text{Fuel}_{\text{saved}}$)
* **Definition:** Quantifies the uncombusted diesel fuel saved by eliminating stationary truck idling and active reefer cooling burn during queue holds.
* **Calculation:**
  $$\text{Fuel}_{\text{saved}} = T_{\text{saved}} \times R_{\text{idle}}$$
* **Variables & Inputs:**
  * $R_{\text{idle}} = 2.50\text{ Liters/Hour}$ (Heavy truck idle and auxiliary reefer cooling burn rate, based on Thermo King SB-210 specifications).
  * **Net Impact:** **105.00 Liters of diesel saved per express transit**.

#### 💨 3. $\text{CO}_2$ Emissions Avoided ($M_{\text{CO}_2}$)
* **Definition:** Calculates the direct reduction in carbon dioxide emissions resulting from avoided fuel burn.
* **Calculation:**
  $$M_{\text{CO}_2} = \text{Fuel}_{\text{saved}} \times \text{EF}_{\text{diesel}}$$
* **Variables & Inputs:**
  * $\text{EF}_{\text{diesel}} = 2.68\text{ kg CO}_2/\text{Liter}$ (Recognized European Environment Agency / DEFRA standard emission factor for diesel combustion).
  * **Net Impact:** **281.40 kg $\text{CO}_2$ avoided per express transit**.

#### ⚡ 4. Operational Efficiency Gain ($\text{Eff}_{\text{gain}}$)
* **Definition:** Tracks the percentage improvement in corridor throughput and administrative processing speed.
* **Calculation:**
  $$\text{Eff}_{\text{gain}} = \left( \frac{T_{\text{baseline}} - T_{\text{pass}}}{T_{\text{baseline}}} \right) \times 100$$
* **Variables & Inputs:**
  * Evaluated continuously by the sub-500ms Node.js decision engine.
  * **Net Impact:** **>98.8% latency reduction** for pre-cleared, weight-compliant freight units.

#### 💶 5. Resource & ESG Financial Efficiency ($\text{Cost}_{\text{ESG}}$)
* **Definition:** Translates physical energy and emissions savings into economic terms, quantifying avoided carbon tax exposure and preserved cargo value.
* **Calculation:**
  $$\text{Cost}_{\text{ESG}} = \left( \frac{M_{\text{CO}_2}}{1000} \times C_{\text{quota}} \right) + (\text{Fuel}_{\text{saved}} \times P_{\text{diesel}})$$
* **Variables & Inputs:**
  * $C_{\text{quota}} = \text{€80.00 / Tonne CO}_2$ (ICE Dec Carbon Futures Index baseline).
  * $P_{\text{diesel}} = \text{€1.50 / Liter}$ (EU commercial diesel price benchmark).
  * **Net Impact:** Direct economic savings embedded into audit-ready Scope 3 ESG compliance certificates.

